  "plan": "InstinctFlash plan for nvidia/GR00T-N1.7-3B\n  plan tier: BITEXACT\n  operating point: schedule {backbone=1 + action=4} | guidance {action=none@1 [implied by mode]} | cfg batching {batch-1 on all 5 declared forwards (no stream requests a negative branch)}\n\n  APPLY  graph_capture              [BITEXACT  ] no stream persists, so every cycle presents identical shapes, so one capture serves every cycle; 5 forward(s) per control step (backbone=1 + action=4) each pay full dispatch cost today; GR00T N1.7 native NFE=4 on Thor: paired and repeated 2026-09-11 DiT graph measurements preserved finite action bytes on the tested checkpoint and inputs, with modest latency gains; see eval/groot_native_graphs_2026-09-11. Only the existing DiT graph is admitted here, not experimental text-block fusions. The family startup exact self-check still decides admission for this process.\n         expected: removes per-forward dispatch cost where the region is replay-safe. Measured ON pi05 (H100, pi05_base, 50-step chunk): a denoise step is 2187 kernel launches, 17.25 ms of CPU submit against 9.48 ms of GPU work -- 99.9% submit-bound, the GPU idle ~45% of the step. The naive region (per-step DynamicCache clone+append) replays fast and WRONG and stays discarded; the static-KV region (pi05_iwm/static_capture.py) is replay-safe by construction and collected the prize: denoise step 16.25 -> 4.57 ms (3.55x), chunk 298.7 -> 181.3 ms (1.65x), bitexact on unseen inputs and prompts. Both halves are this model's -- a backbone whose forwards are already compute-bound has nothing here to win either way, so measure the submit-vs-busy split, then measure replay against eager on a SECOND input\n         decision: graph_capture: self-check bit-exact on 6 inputs (replay == eager exactly; staged 6 fresh-inputs (all float tensors redrawn); 0.2 s startup cost, once per process)\n  skip   engine_offload             [NUMERIC   ] precision='native': FP8 engine is not authorized; legal but tier NUMERIC exceeds ceiling BITEXACT: SM110: FP8 engine passes the declared dimension and denoise checks; action-horizon and observation/control compatibility still require validation; baked denoise operating point: action=4 steps; guidance action=none@1\n  skip   pi05_tf32_numeric          [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:pi05', 'declares:pi05_tf32_numeric']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   fsdp_elision               [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   allocator_churn_elision    [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   debug_dump_elision         [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   obs_decode_elision         [BITEXACT  ] model declares no observation-decode modules\n  skip   conditioning_prefill       [BITEXACT  ] ['backbone_features'] is chunk- or episode-constant, but the model's own implementation already hoists it out of the loop, so there is nothing to hoist\n  skip   prompt_encoder_staging     [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   ring_kv_addressing         [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   action_terminal_forward_elision [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILITY decision, not a recipe one.\n  skip   sm120_gated_residual       [BITEXACT  ] checkpoint does not declare ['backbone:wan_va']; the pass is not applicable to it. This is a CAPABILIT